      "math_academy_id": "q-316961",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
